{
  "id": "think-aloud-protocol",
  "term": "think-aloud protocol",
  "definition": "A think-aloud protocol is a method in which people verbalize their thinking as close as possible to real time while doing or considering a task. It is used to capture a more faithful account of what they are thinking and to reduce problems linked to memory, estimation, and ambiguous self-report.",
